{:id :EACL-FORMAL-091
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust/EACL-RS-107/default-limits-codec-ceiling"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :other
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0.0 commit a698b3bdf15e61be9bfd1324d7d7c67dc82176be"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "check-expression-bytes! measured a permission's payload by rendering it through expression/encode, which applies the canonical codec's 262,144-entry and 1 MiB ceilings before the typed comparison with :maximum-expression-bytes (131,072 by default). A permission whose resolved arrows or relations span many subject types exceeded a codec ceiling first, so schema admission raised :eacl.format/invalid :too-large or :too-many-entries instead of :eacl.schema/expression-limit :encoded-byte-size, with default limits."
 :fix
 "Measure the payload with expression/encoded-byte-size, the exact UTF-8 size of the canonical encoding computed without rendering or codec ceilings, so the typed limit decides and reports the exact actual size."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.schema.expression-limits-test/encoded-byte-limit-precedes-codec-ceilings-test"
  "eacl.schema.expression-test/encoded-byte-size-matches-the-canonical-encoding-test"]
 :notes
 "Found by the eacl-rust port (BUGS.md EACL-RS-107), verified against main a698b3bd."}
